{\*\generator Msftedit 5.41.21.2510;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 P?S/8 System Programs Directory Internal Structures\par
\par
Last edit:  04-Jun-2018 cjl\par
\par
Unlike most PDP-8 operating systems, P?S/8 maintains a separate directory for core-image system programs.  This allows highly specialized entries tailored to the individual requirements of each program.  This includes certain command-line parsing variations and the ability to maintain internal program overlays.  The P?S/8 command-line mechanism supports many features that are akin to Concise Command Language [CCL] as implemented in other systems with system-specific variations.  Certain aspects of the commands are managed by control bits in the entries for each system program; this is especially crucial regarding programs implemented as overlays to the keyboard monitor.\par
\par
Figure 1 shows the entire System Programs directory particular to the TC01/TC08 configuration and includes all specific program details.  Note: This listing can be obtained using the P?S/8 \i DIRECT \i0 program with the /S command-line option switch (and possibly additional options) set; for more information, consult separate documentation of P?S/8 DIRECT.\f1\par
\par
